// PSS v3.0 LRM — Example 57: Anonymous action traversal (page 132)
action A {
  rand bit[3:0]   f1;
}
action B {
  A a1, a2;

  activity {
    a1;
    a2 with {
      f1 < 10;
    };
  }
}
action A {
  rand bit[3:0]   f1;
}
action B {
  activity {
    do A;
    do A with {f1 < 10;};
  }
}

Example 58 shows the use of a label of an action traversal statement to constrain a sub-action instance from
a higher activity context.
